        <body>
            <div xml:id="d811">

                <pb facs="0787" n="689" sameAs="frus:frus1900/pg689"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hay to Mr.
                            Hunter.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1900-05-24"><hi rendition="#italic">May 24,
                        1900</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 251.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to instruction No. 236, of March
                    20 last, directing you to inform the Government of Honduras that the Government
                    of the United States insists upon the payment of an indemnity of $10,000 for the
                    murder of Frank Pears, I have now to inquire if the Government of Honduras has
                    made answer to that demand? If it has not, you will remind it of the importance
                    of the matter.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John Hay.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
